--- [2] FAILING-FIRST PROOF (pre-fix) ---
Command: MIX_ENV=test mix test test/hiraeth/real_catalog_importer_test.exs:127 --trace
Result: exit 2, 12 tests, 1 failure, 11 excluded. The red assertion reproduced:
  Assertion with == failed
  code:  assert length(Ash.read!(ImportRun, authorize?: false)) == first_import_runs + 1
  left:  2
  right: 3
  (test/hiraeth/real_catalog_importer_test.exs:149)
This matches the plan's premise exactly (2 != 3): the second seed! pass reuses
the provider's existing applied ImportRun (ensure_import_run! find-or-create
on provider+status=="applied", fresh per-call cache), so the count stays at
first_import_runs and the working-tree `+ 1` assertion is red. The seed_provider
TASK's always-create behavior is separate (its own test asserts 2 runs after 2
invocations) and stays untouched.
NOTE: the line-127 run also surfaced unused-alias warnings in this file
(Series, SeriesMembership, SourceLedgerEntry) — introduced by the working-tree
monster split; assessed below for gate/credo impact.

